⟦⎊⟧ TPR setup — the journey a new user actually walks
⋮⋮TPR.HUB⋮⋮
⧗-26.392 · every "have" below was checked on the running system

The rule that shapes all of it: :7090 is the first thing a person
sees after login. The face is the product; the bot is the door to it.

── 0 · THE GATE (do this first, it is not a feature) ──────────

  Right now /api/tier and /api/clear are on the public funnel with
  NO auth. A POST from anyone on the internet can switch the tier
  — including RunPod tiers that bill $1.22-$21.76/hr — or wipe the
  conversation spool. The mini app reads `initDataUnsafe`, which is
  the client's word for who it is, unverified.

  Login IS the gate:
    · validate Telegram initData: HMAC-SHA256 over the sorted data
      string, key = SHA256("WebAppData" + bot_token) — server side
    · reject anything older than a few minutes (auth_date)
    · issue a short session cookie; /api/* requires it
    · anything a stranger must never touch moves to :5090, which
      is not on the funnel at all
  Have: nothing. This is the first build.
:: ∎

── 1 · FIND ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  They search @tpr_zenbot, or someone forwards them a group.
  Have: bot exists (id 8305423651), name TelePromptR, groups on,
  commands pushed to all four scopes.
  Missing: the about + description are still empty — the first
  screen a stranger reads. Copy is drafted in
  ZenBots/TelePromptR/copy.txt, held until Lucius approves.
:: ∎

── 2 · /start IN A DM ─────────────────────────────────────────
  Two buttons, nothing else:
    [ Add TPR to a group ]   → t.me/tpr_zenbot?startgroup=true
    [ Open TPR ]             → the mini app at :7090
  Have: /start exists but answers with Ender's copy and no buttons.
:: ∎

── 3 · ADD TO A GROUP ─────────────────────────────────────────
  The moment TPR lands in a room it should say what it needs:
  turn Topics on, and name the first topic.
  Have: `my_chat_member` is now in allowed_updates, so Telegram
  WILL send the event. Nothing handles it yet.
  Missing: the handler, and the group card it should write
  (Pulse/tpr/Groups/<name>/group.me) so the room is known.
:: ∎

── 4 · LOGIN ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Tapping [ Open TPR ] opens the mini app; Telegram hands it
  initData; the face verifies it (step 0) and now knows the person.
  Have: the mini app loads publicly — /tpr/app returns 200 — and
  webapp/tpr.html is already built in the ZENSEN palette.
  Missing: the verification, and therefore the login.
:: ∎

── 5 · LAND ON :7090 ──────────────────────────────────────────
  The first screen. It answers four questions without being asked:
    who am I          the Telegram identity that just logged in
    where am I        the rooms TPR shares with me, topics listed
    who answers       the being bound to each topic, and on what
    is it alive       seat readiness, pulled from the brains
  The face does not compute the last one — it asks :5090/readiness,
  which probes the seats for real. That is the whole reason the
  brains is a separate door.
  Have: the page, the palette, and a live /readiness on the brains.
  Missing: the four panels, and the session that makes them mean
  anything.
:: ∎

── 6 · NAME A TOPIC ───────────────────────────────────────────
  A topic with a card is a conversation with a being. Today that
  means editing files on the box; a new user cannot do that.
  From the face: name the topic, pick the being, pick the metal.
  Have: the card system works end to end — cards are read into the
  prompt, the being resolves, the tier pins, the desk is scoped.
  Missing: writing a card from the face instead of from a shell.
:: ∎

── 7 · TALK ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  CORRECTED ⧗-26.392 — I wrote "done" here and it was wrong. What
  is done belongs to @ender_zenbot, a DIFFERENT bot that has been
  running for months. For @tpr_zenbot the honest state is: the bot
  was created and added to a group, and nothing else.
  Have now: its own process on :7098, identity confirmed by getMe,
  webhook registered at /tprbot.
  Missing: the funnel path /tprbot. Until it exists Telegram has
  nowhere to deliver, so the bot sits in the group and says nothing.
  That single path is the difference between a bot and a member.
:: ∎

── BUILD ORDER · smallest first, each one testable alone ──────
  1 initData verification + session  → the gate (step 0)
  2 /api/* behind the session; the dangerous ones move to :5090
  3 /start with the two buttons      → step 2
  4 my_chat_member handler           → step 3, the "add me" moment
  5 the four panels on :7090         → step 5, the product
  6 write a topic card from the face → step 6
  7 a process for @tpr_zenbot        → it has a token and no seat

  Nothing above needs the brains to grow. When it does grow, the
  next thing it takes is DELIVER — the model call itself — and the
  face becomes a thin Telegram adapter, which is the point.
:: ∎
